 {
  "id": "M27/p4",
  "lesson": "M27",
  "kind": "prediction",
  "prompt": "<p>You estimate the entropy of an 8-outcome distribution by plugging in the empirical frequencies of 20 samples. On average, compared with the true entropy, the estimate is:</p>",
  "answer": "a",
  "answerKind": "choice",
  "tol": 0,
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "a",
    "html": "<p>too low</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "b",
    "html": "<p>too high</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "c",
    "html": "<p>unbiased</p>"
   },
   {
    "key": "d",
    "html": "<p>too low or too high with equal probability</p>"
   }
  ],
  "explain": "<p>Too low. With 20 samples some outcomes are missing and the observed frequencies are lumpier than the truth, and lumpier distributions have lower entropy. (Formally, entropy is concave, so by Jensen's inequality the expected plug-in value is below the entropy of the expected frequencies.)</p>"
 },
 {
